advsimp=&quot;Simple&quot;

movement_int=.5 --surprisingly enough, movement_*int* is not actually an integer. Set it to be any positive number. Negative numbers will make the tool impossible to move bricks with. :P I suggest keeping numbers from .25 to 1. There&apos;s no reason in most cases to go above 1. If you go below .25, the handles object might not work well.
rotate_rounding=5 --rounds off to &lt;x&gt; degree intervals.

--&quot;move&quot;,&quot;save&quot;,&quot;delete&quot;,&quot;color&quot;,&quot;lock&quot;,&quot;change material of&quot;,&quot;change surface of&quot;,&quot;change transparency of&quot;,&quot;change reflectance of&quot;

--DONE: Fix up the permissions board. Make the up and down buttons go up and down, as well as make the &apos;permissions given to you&apos; and &apos;permissions given to others&apos; buttons work.
--DONE: Finish the Mesh Editor. Let users change textureId and MeshId from the script.
--TO DO: Add an option to enable and disable shortcuts, as well as a way to input what number to round when rotating
--TO DO: Allow players to turn the axis bricks on and off.
--TO DO: Add images for each of the buttons.
--TO DO: Add a help database. Oh god. &gt;_&gt;

